==Battleground==
*1 [[Vega (Enemy)|Vega]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Guile (Enemy)|Guile]] spawns after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Chun-Li (Enemy)|Chun-Li]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*5 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*8 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The bosses in this level are a bit more buffed than usual Street Fighter stages. However, it compensates with peons that are easy to deal with and drop a lot of money, so you should focus on the bosses for this stage. Don't bring Cats with too high range, as Vega will make them highly ineffective. [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] fits that criteria greatly, along with his [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed variants]]. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat's]] range is very useful here.

It is also possible to rush the stage and destroy the base before any fighter appears by spamming rushers like [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion]], or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] once Kang Roo is killed.

